messages:
patricia: Heads-up team: publishing the "Breaking Change Policy v2" doc in 30m. It's focused on edge cases (minor->major renames, param semantic shifts) and includes a recommended rollout checklist for SDKs and Docs. Please skim.
julio: Nice. Does v2 change the standard 60/180 timeline or add exceptions?
emma: Core timeline unchanged (60-day soft, 180-day hard), but v2 formalizes an "exception path" for semantic changes where we provide compatibility adapters, extra telemetry windows, and partner escalation for Dedicated/Private customers.
docs-bot: Docs build passed -> staging (build 5235) :white_check_mark: Link: https://internal.redwood.dev/docs/breaking-change-policy-v2
yana: Two asks: 1) add a codemod example for API surface renames (simple rename + API key check). 2) make sure we include a small runtime shim snippet for Node and Python.
qasim: On the shim: we implemented a lightweight header-mapping shim that maps X-RW-Old-Param -> X-RW-New-Param and logs sdk.compatibility.shim_used telemetry. Should we publish that code?
patricia: Yes, include a safe, audited example in the playbook but don't publish the service implementation. Just the client-side shim and config flags.
emma: Added code samples — short Node example:

```
// shim example (node)
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  // map legacy query param to new name
  if (req.url.includes('max_tokens_rev')) {
    req.url = req.url.replace('max_tokens_rev', 'max_output_tokens');
    console.log('shim: mapped max_tokens_rev -> max_output_tokens');
  }
  // proxy request downstream...
});
```

and a Python wrapper for the SDK client that normalizes kwargs.
julio: Can we add a checklist for when a change is considered "semantic" vs "cosmetic"? This keeps folks from using exception path improperly.
patricia: Good call. v2 includes a quick decision flow: semantic if responses change meaning or tokenization; cosmetic if only parameter names/aliases. Semantic changes require a design review and partner outreach.
legal: Please include language about contractually required timelines: Dedicated customers with SLA addenda can request 6-12 month extensions. Added the paragraph and a link to the Account escalation template.
qasim: Telemetry: we recommend emitting three tags for migrations: `sdk.breaking.announce`, `sdk.breaking.adoption`, and `sdk.compat.shim_used`. Docs includes sample queries for migration dashboards.
ya na: small nit: the docs link for sample grep/sed codemod is missing. can you add a safe sed snippet and a note about false positives?patricia: Added sed and a jscodeshift codemod example, plus guidance to run in a branch and CI. Example sed: `git grep -l "max_tokens_rev" | xargs sed -i 's/max_tokens_rev/max_output_tokens/g'` with caveats about string literals.
emma: Also added a short test harness snippet to validate parity: generate with old param and new param and assert hash(headers+first_token) equal.
docs-bot: Announcement draft saved: https://internal.redwood.dev/announcements/breaking-change-policy-v2-draft. Schedule: post to #sdk-announcements and #docs at 11:00 PT.
julio: For partner communication: can we auto-generate a CSV of affected repos using telemetry (top callers of deprecated param)? would help AMs.
qasim: We have a query ready. Docs references the exact query and a sample CSV export process.
legal: One compliance note: add explicit guidance for GDPR regions about telemetry retention and opt-out during migration windows. We added the clause.
patricia: Great. If no objections I'll publish in 30m and ping Partnerships and Account teams to start outreach. emoji :rocket:
qasim: No objections from infra. I'll add the migration dashboard to the SLO tracking board after publish.
emma: Thanks all. Small follow-up: will we create a public version of the FAQ for external users?patricia: Yes, external FAQ will be shorter, linking to migration recipes and contact points. Internal playbook remains the canonical doc."
